 "transcript": "Captions file of 20260922_C5070.MP4 (Shannon Who Gives Interview, Bryant Park, 22 Sep 2026). Times are mm:ss.ms in the source file. Nick Reis asks the questions off camera. The auto speaker labels in the Google Doc are wrong, so none are given here. Her name, state, job title and company (00:05–00:12) are left out: never use them.\n[00:00.0] Okay, so first question I have for you, can you just introduce yourself for me?\n[00:13.5] Awesome, thank you Shannon.\n[00:14.9] So first question I have for you, can you finish the sentence, who gives blank or what comes to mind when you hear who gives?\n[00:24.6] When I think about who gives, the first thing that comes to mind is everyone should be giving\n[00:28.6] if they're not, so yeah you should give.\n[00:32.8] Awesome and why do you think it's important for people to give?\n[00:36.8] It's important for people to give so that they can have an impact in the world and be\n[00:40.1] a part of something bigger than themselves.\n[00:42.8] Exactly, can you think of a time where you like gave back like you know either time or money or volunteer to an organization that really stuck with you and showed you why giving is so important?\n[00:55.3] There's a lot of organizations out there that I'm very passionate about and that I like\n[00:59.3] to give whether it's my time, my talents, or my treasures but Watsi is certainly at\n[01:04.7] the top of that list.\n[01:06.4] Amazing and last thing maybe you know like start a sentence with who gives and then just finish the sentence from there if you could think of anything.\n[01:16.9] Let me think about that one one more time.\n[01:27.2] Alright, who gives to make a difference?\n[01:30.6] Perfect and one other question I just thought of for you, are you happy?\n[01:34.9] I'm happy, absolutely.\n[01:37.5] And why are you happy?\n[01:39.2] I'm happy because I go to sleep every night knowing that the work that I do is touching\n[01:43.2] someone else's life.\n[01:44.6] Amazing, alright that's all we got for you right there.\n[01:47.0] Thanks."
